Description: Color FX buttons pick what the FILTER knobs do
 Four Pioneer SOUND COLOR FX for both decks' FILTER knobs, which drive the
 decks' QuickEffect chains (super1): SPACE (reverb), DUB ECHO (half-beat
 echo with long feedback), NOISE (white noise) and FILTER (the filter alone,
 as before). Each is silent with the knob at the centre, the effect rising
 towards either end, over the Pioneered Filter's low-pass (left) / high-pass
 (right) sweep. New ColorFxControl (src/effects/colorfxcontrol.{h,cpp}),
 owned by EffectsManager, builds the chains itself from the effects'
 manifest defaults -- effect first, filter second, the effect's amount
 linked LINKED_LEFT_RIGHT -- so they do not depend on the QuickEffect preset
 list in the preferences. Controls [Pioneered],color_fx_space / _dub_echo /
 _noise / _filter read 1 while selected; a request for 1 selects, a request
 for 0 is refused, so plain two-state skin buttons act as radio buttons.
 Switching keeps the super knob where the hardware knob is. The choice is
 written to mixxx.cfg ([Pioneered] ColorFx) and flushed at once, and is
 applied after effects.xml is read at startup and to decks added later.
 .
 White Noise is now centred on zero (-0.5..0.5 instead of 0..1, same
 peak-to-peak level). The old noise rode on a DC offset of half full scale,
 which a low-pass after it turns into a large DC step into the amplifier.
